@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Capability / Effect Authorization
' Paper: Miller, Robust Composition — Object-Capability Model (JHU 2006)
' URL:   https://papers.agoric.com/assets/pdf/papers/robust-composition.pdf
' URL:   http://web.archive.org/web/20260423141335/http://www.erights.org/talks/thesis/markm-thesis.pdf
' Formerly: cited as http://www.erights.org/talks/thesis/markm-thesis.pdf — dead as of 2026-09-01
'           (HTTP 500 on three tries; the whole of erights.org is down, root included). Replaced with
'           the author-affiliated host — Agoric, where Miller is Chief Scientist — verified to be the
'           same JHU dissertation, May 2006. The Wayback snapshot above is the last known-good copy of
'           the original URL (captured 2026-04-23).
' Paper: Saltzer & Schroeder, The Protection of Information in Computer Systems, 1975
' URL:   https://web.mit.edu/Saltzer/www/publications/protection/
' Level: 4
' Provenance: projects/aphelion · effectauth/effectauth.go, commandeffect/plan.go

cloud     "Model proposal\n(command / action)"             as M    <<cloud>>
component "Command-effect classifier"                      as CLS  <<app>>
component "Capability check\n(granted work-mode)"          as GATE <<app>>
component "Capability grant\n(scope · work-mode · expiry)" as CAP  <<db>>
component "Effect executed"                                as EXE  <<app>>
component "Denied"                                         as DEN  <<error>>

M    ARROW_CLOUD    CLS  : proposes
CLS  ARROW_MAIN     GATE : effect kind
CAP  ARROW_OPTIONAL GATE : active grant
GATE ARROW_MAIN     EXE  : within granted work-mode
GATE ARROW_ERROR    DEN  : exceeds capability

note bottom of CAP
  Work-mode ladder: read_only < workspace_write < commit < deploy.
  Authority is a **first-class object** — auditable, expirable,
  narrowable; the proposal never widens it (least privilege).
end note
@enduml
